  "mechanismSummary": "The nitro group withdraws electrons, so nitrobenzene reacts much more slowly than benzene (hence the harsh conditions). After ortho or para attack one resonance form would put the positive charge on the carbon bearing the already positive nitrogen: very unfavourable. Meta attack avoids that form, so meta is the least bad choice: 1,3-dinitrobenzene is the major product.",
